  abstract = {The study compares statistical and machine-learning species distribution models for freshwater macroinvertebrates in Swiss rivers. It evaluates predictive performance, overfitting, out-of-domain generalization, and response-shape interpretation across multiple model classes. The analysis shows that quantifying overfitting helps interpret model behavior and can reveal when flexible predictive models produce unreliable ecological response patterns.},
